module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SliceExteriorAlgebraSheafification
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.KoszulUnitCover
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulSelfExtGluingChain

/-!
# The self-Ext comparison on all of a ringed space

Let `Y` be a ringed space, `𝓘 ⊆ O_Y` a sheaf of ideals and `O_X = O_Y/𝓘`.  The local statements
of [Stacks, Tag 0BQY] live over an open `U` on which `𝓘` is generated by sections whose Koszul
complex is acyclic in positive degrees; this file glues them into one statement on `Y`.

Two inputs make the gluing possible.  The first is a cover of **all** of `Y` by such opens, which
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.coversTop_koszulPresentationOpen` supplies for a
Koszul-regular sheaf of ideals; the second is the conclusion of the tag over one member of that
cover, which is
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isExteriorAlgebra_genOver_descend_koszul`.  The
gluing itself is `SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.IsExteriorAlgebra.isIso_desc_app_of_coversTop`:
the comparison a square-zero degree-one generator induces out of an exterior algebra is an
isomorphism in every degree as soon as both algebras restrict to exterior algebras over the
members of a covering family.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.KoszulPresentation`: an open of `Y` together with
  a sequence of sections generating `𝓘` over it whose Koszul complex is acyclic in positive
  degrees.  The index type of the cover: carrying the sequence in the index rather than
  recovering it from an existential is what lets the per-member inputs of the gluing be stated.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.iSup_koszulPresentation_eq_top` and
  `coversTop_koszulPresentation`: for a Koszul-regular sheaf of ideals the opens carrying a
  Koszul presentation cover `Y`, indexed by `KoszulPresentation`.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isExteriorAlgebra_genOver_descend_presentation`:
  the hypothesis `hBV` of the gluing at one member of that cover, with the Koszul chain datum
  and its quasi-isomorphism built from the member's own sequence.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.squareZero_id_descend_koszulRegular`: the
  degree-one generator of the descended composition-product algebra has square zero on all of
  `Y` — the one hypothesis the comparison map out of an exterior algebra needs.
* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isIso_desc_app_koszulRegular`: **the comparison
  `⋀ⁿ(Ext¹(O_X, O_X)) ⟶ Extⁿ(O_X, O_X)` is an isomorphism in every degree `n` on all of `Y`**,
  for the descended composition-product algebra of a K-injective resolution of the quotient.

## Implementation notes

**The sheaf of rings the quotient is presented at is named once.**
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceExterior.isExteriorAlgebra_over`, which supplies the hypothesis
`hAV`, is stated for a sheaf of modules over `CategoryTheory.Sheaf.toRingCat J Osharp` with
`Osharp` a sheaf of commutative rings, while the descended composition-product algebra lives over
a bare sheaf of rings.  The quotient is therefore carried as a sheaf of commutative rings
`Osharp` throughout and the sheaf of rings it is read at is written `toRingCat _ Osharp` and
nothing else; a second spelling of one sheaf of rings is what sends the elaborator into the
sheafified coproduct of a free sheaf of modules.

**Three inputs are carried as hypotheses, and each is an identification and not a gap in the
gluing.**  The annihilation of every homogeneous piece of the composition-product algebra of the
resolution by the kernel of the quotient map is what makes the descent of that algebra exist at
all, so it appears in the statement; it is the global counterpart of
`Stacks.RegularSequence.KoszulChainData.smul_homologyPiece_eq_zero`, and is discharged by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.smul_globalHomologyPiece_eq_zero` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulSelfExtGlobalAnnihilation`.  The other two
are the member-by-member identifications the chain of presentations consumes: that the member's
sequence generates, over the objects of `Opens Y / U`, the sheaf of ideals the global morphism
generates, and that the quotient of the structure sheaf over `U` by that sequence is the
restriction of the global quotient.  Both are read off the generation hypothesis carried in
`KoszulPresentation`, the first by
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sectionIdeal_sliceIdealOfSections_eq` and the second
by `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.sliceQuotientRingHom`.

**No `@[stacks]` attribute.** The conclusion below is the tag's comparison for the *descended
composition-product algebra* of a chosen resolution, and three of its hypotheses are
identifications rather than the tag's own.  Instantiated at the chosen K-injective resolution of
the quotient and at those three, it becomes the tag's global statement, which is where the tag is
registered: `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isIso_desc_app_isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf`
of `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularSequence.KoszulSelfExtKoszulRegular`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BQY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BQY)
* [Stacks Project, Definition 31.21.2 (Tag 063D)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/063D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A8V](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A8V)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A91](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A91)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Sheaf Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry HomologicalComplex Stacks.ChainComplex

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

open Stacks.Sites Stacks.SheafOfModules Stacks.RegularSequence
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasiRegular
open Stacks.RingedSpace
open _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-! ### The cover, with its sequences carried in the index -/

/-- **A Koszul presentation of a sheaf of ideals**: an open `U` of `Y` together with sections
`f₁, …, f_r` of `O_Y` over `U` generating the sheaf of ideals there whose Koszul complex is
acyclic in positive degrees.  This is the local hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 063D] part (2) with
the witnessing sequence kept.

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.KoszulPresentationOpen` is the same notion with the
sequence hidden behind an existential.  The gluing needs it in the open: each member of the cover
supplies the comparisons of the chain of presentations, and those comparisons are statements
about the sequence. -/
structure KoszulPresentation (Y : RingedSpace.{u, u})
    (J : (structureSheafModule Y).Submodule) where
  /-- The open of `Y` over which the presentation lives. -/
  U : Opens Y.carrier
  /-- The length of the generating sequence. -/
  r : ℕ
  /-- The generating sequence of sections of `O_Y` over `U`. -/
  f : Fin r → Y.presheaf.obj (op U)
  /-- The Koszul complex of the sequence is acyclic in positive degrees. -/
  koszulExact : IsKoszulSequenceExactOn Y U f (fun j => 0 < j)
  /-- The sequence generates the sheaf of ideals over `U`. -/
  generated : IsGeneratedByOn Y J U f

section Cover

variable {Y : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (J : (structureSheafModule Y).Submodule)

/-- **The opens carrying a Koszul presentation of a Koszul-regular sheaf of ideals exhaust
`Y`.** Every point lies in one of them, by
`exists_koszulPresentation_of_isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf`, whose witnessing sequence is the one the
index records. -/
theorem iSup_koszulPresentation_eq_top (hJ : IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf Y J) :
    (⨆ d : KoszulPresentation Y J, d.U) = ⊤ := by
  refine SetLike.ext fun x => ⟨fun _ => Opens.mem_top x, fun _ => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, r, f, hkos, hgen⟩ :=
    exists_koszulPresentation_of_isKoszulRegularIdealSheaf J hJ x
  exact Opens.mem_iSup.mpr ⟨⟨U, r, f, hkos, hgen⟩, hxU⟩

/-- **A Koszul-regular sheaf of ideals admits a Koszul presentation on a cover of all of `Y`**,
indexed by the presentations themselves.  This is the covering family the gluing of
[Stacks, Tag 0BQY] runs over. -/
theorem coversTop_koszulPresentation (hJ : IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf Y J) :
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier).CoversTop
      (fun d : KoszulPresentation Y J => d.U) :=
  (Opens.coversTop_iff _ _).mpr (IsOpenCover.mk (iSup_koszulPresentation_eq_top J hJ))

end Cover

/-! ### The gluing -/

section Glue

variable {Y : RingedSpace.{u, u}} (J : (structureSheafModule Y).Submodule)
  [HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [(Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : Opens Y.carrier,
    HasSheafify ((Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier).over V) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : Opens Y.carrier,
    ((Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier).over V).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : Opens Y.carrier, HasSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥V) AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : Opens Y.carrier,
    (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥V).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : Opens Y.carrier, HasWeakSheafify (Opens.grothendieckTopology ↥V) CommRingCat.{u}]
  [∀ V : Opens Y.carrier,
    HasWeakSheafify ((Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier).over V) CommRingCat.{u}]
  {F : _root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing Y)}
  (Φ : F ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing Y))
  (Q : CochainComplex (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u}
    (structureSheafRing Y)) ℤ) (hQ : Q.IsKInjective)
  (e : DerivedCategory.Q.obj
      ((single (_root_.SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing Y))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).obj (cokernel Φ)) ≅
    DerivedCategory.Q.obj Q)
  {Osharp : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) CommRingCat.{u}}
  (α : structureSheafRing Y ⟶
    toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) Osharp)
  [hαloc : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) α.hom]
  (hAglob : ∀ (n : ℤ) (W : (Opens Y.carrier)ᵒᵖ)
      (b : (structureSheafRing Y).obj.obj W),
    b ∈ RingHom.ker (α.hom.app W).hom →
      ∀ m : ((globalHomologyGradedAlgebra Q).piece n).val.obj W, b • m = 0)
  (hgen : ∀ d : KoszulPresentation Y J, ∀ W : (Over d.U)ᵒᵖ,
    sectionIdeal (sliceIdealOfSections d.U d.f) W =
      sectionIdeal (idealOfHom (O := Y.sheaf.over d.U)
        ((_root_.SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u}
          (structureSheafRing Y) d.U).map Φ)) W)
  (θ : ∀ d : KoszulPresentation Y J,
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf.{u, u, u}
        (quotientRingSheaf.{u, u, u} (sliceIdealOfSections d.U d.f)) ⟶
      (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) Osharp).over d.U)
  (hθloc : ∀ d : KoszulPresentation Y J,
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective ((Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier).over d.U) (θ d).hom)
  (hθ : ∀ d : KoszulPresentation Y J,
    quotientRingHom (sliceIdealOfSections d.U d.f) ≫ θ d = overRingHom α d.U)

/-- **The composition-product algebra of a K-injective resolution of the quotient, descended
along the quotient map.**  The sheaf of graded algebras on `Y` whose degree-`n` piece is
`Extⁿ(O_X, O_X)` and whose multiplication is composition, read as an algebra over `O_X` rather
than over `O_Y`. -/
abbrev descendedSelfExtAlgebra : _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u}
    (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) Osharp) :=
  descend α (globalHomologyGradedAlgebra Q) hAglob

include hgen hQ e hθloc hθ in
/-- **The hypothesis `hBV` of the gluing, at one member of the cover.**  Over the open of a
Koszul presentation the restriction of the descended composition-product algebra of the
resolution is the exterior algebra of its own degree-one piece.

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf.isExteriorAlgebra_genOver_descend_koszul` is the
statement; what is supplied here is its Koszul chain datum, namely
`Stacks.RegularSequence.koszulChainData` of the Koszul morphism of the member's own sequence read
on the open subspace, together with the quasi-isomorphism of its augmentation — which is the
member's acyclicity hypothesis, carried to the augmentation by
`Stacks.RegularSequence.quasiIso_koszulAugmentation_restrict` and converted to the spelling
instance search needs by
`Stacks.RegularSequence.quasiIso_koszulChainData_augmentation`. -/
theorem isExteriorAlgebra_genOver_descend_presentation (d : KoszulPresentation Y J) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.IsExteriorAlgebra
      ((descendedSelfExtAlgebra Q α hAglob).over d.U)
      (genOver (𝟙 ((descendedSelfExtAlgebra Q α hAglob).piece 1)) d.U) :=
  have := hθloc d
  have : QuasiIso (koszulChainData (koszulHomOfSections (openSubspace d.U).sheaf
      fun j => sectionOnRestriction Y d.U (d.f j))).augmentation :=
    quasiIso_koszulChainData_augmentation _
      (quasiIso_koszulAugmentation_restrict Y d.U d.f d.koszulExact)
  isExteriorAlgebra_genOver_descend_koszul d.U d.f
    (koszulChainData (koszulHomOfSections (openSubspace d.U).sheaf
      fun j => sectionOnRestriction Y d.U (d.f j)))
    Φ (hgen d) Q hQ e α hAglob (θ d) (hθ d)

include hgen hQ e hθloc hθ in
/-- **The degree-one generator of the descended composition-product algebra has square zero on
all of `Y`.**  The square-zero condition is local on the site
(`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.SquareZero.of_coversTop`), and over each member of the cover it
is the first half of the universal property established there. -/
theorem squareZero_id_descend_koszulRegular (hJ : IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf Y J) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.SquareZero
      (𝟙 ((descendedSelfExtAlgebra Q α hAglob).piece 1)) :=
  SquareZero.of_coversTop (coversTop_koszulPresentation J hJ) fun d =>
    (isExteriorAlgebra_genOver_descend_presentation J Φ Q hQ e α hAglob hgen θ hθloc hθ d).1

include hgen hQ e hθloc hθ in
/-- **The comparison of [Stacks, Tag 0BQY] is an isomorphism in every degree on all of `Y`.**
Let `Y` be a ringed space, `𝓘 ⊆ O_Y` a Koszul-regular sheaf of ideals, `O_X = O_Y/𝓘` the
quotient, `Q` a K-injective complex of `O_Y`-modules presenting `O_X`, and `A` with the
degree-one generator `ι` an exterior algebra over `O_X` of `Ext¹(O_X, O_X)`.  Then the
homomorphism of sheaves of graded algebras that the identity of `Ext¹(O_X, O_X)` induces out of
`A` — the comparison composition makes

`⋀ⁿ(Ext¹(O_X, O_X)) ⟶ Extⁿ(O_X, O_X)`

— is an isomorphism in every degree `n`.

The opens carrying a Koszul presentation of `𝓘` cover `Y`
(`coversTop_koszulPresentation`); over each of them the restriction of `A` is again an exterior
algebra of the restricted module
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceExterior.isExteriorAlgebra_over`) and the restriction of the target
is the exterior algebra of its own degree-one piece
(`isExteriorAlgebra_genOver_descend_presentation`); and
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.IsExteriorAlgebra.isIso_desc_app_of_coversTop` glues those two
local statements, restriction to the members of a covering family being jointly conservative on
sheaves of modules. -/
theorem isIso_desc_app_koszulRegular (hJ : IsKoszulRegularIdealSheaf Y J)
    (A : _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.{u, u}
      (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) Osharp))
    (ι : (descendedSelfExtAlgebra Q α hAglob).piece 1 ⟶ A.piece 1)
    (hA : _root_.SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.IsExteriorAlgebra A ι) (n : ℤ) :
    IsIso ((hA.desc (descendedSelfExtAlgebra Q α hAglob)
      (𝟙 ((descendedSelfExtAlgebra Q α hAglob).piece 1))
      (squareZero_id_descend_koszulRegular J Φ Q hQ e α hAglob hgen θ hθloc hθ hJ)).app n) :=
  hA.isIso_desc_app_of_coversTop _ _ (coversTop_koszulPresentation J hJ)
    (fun d => SliceExterior.isExteriorAlgebra_over d.U _ A ι hA)
    (fun d =>
      isExteriorAlgebra_genOver_descend_presentation J Φ Q hQ e α hAglob hgen θ hθloc hθ d) n

end Glue

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RegularIdealSheaf

end
